-- title:
--   Rational depth of horizontal primes in the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\varpi \in W$ be irreducible, and let $e \ge 1$ be a natural number. Write $R = \mathtt{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\varpi^{e})$ for the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ (indexed by `Fin 2`) by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \varpi^{e}$, and let $\mathfrak P$ be a prime of $R$ (an element of `PrimeSpectrum R`, with underlying ideal `P.asIdeal`) subject to two hypotheses: $\mathfrak P \ne 0$, and the class in $R$ of the constant power series $\varpi$, namely `const (ϖ ^ e) ϖ`, does not lie in $\mathfrak P$. The conclusion is the conjunction of three assertions: first, $\operatorname{finrank}_W(R/\mathfrak P) \ge 1$; second, the $W$-module length of $R/(\mathfrak P + (U(\varpi^{e})))$, where $U(\varpi^{e})$ is the element `U (ϖ ^ e)` of $R$ giving one of the two branches of the crossing, is not $\top$, i.e. is finite; and third, there exist natural numbers $r \ge 1$ and $p \ge 1$ with $p + 1 \le re$ and, as an identity in $\mathbb N_\infty$, $$r \cdot \operatorname{length}_W\bigl(R/(\mathfrak P + (U(\varpi^{e})))\bigr) = p \cdot \operatorname{finrank}_W(R/\mathfrak P).$$
--
--   This records that a prime of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^{e})$ which is nonzero and horizontal (does not contain $\varpi$) has a well-defined rational depth $p/r \in (0,e)$ in the annulus attached to the node, measured by the length of the quotient along the branch $U$ against the $W$-rank of the quotient by the prime. It supplies the nondegeneracy and depth data used in the regrouping of orders on a node annulus and in the prolongation-tuple computations of lengths of localized quotients at minimal primes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_mul_length_eq_mul_finrank_of_ne_bot_of_const_notMem.lean

